# User-supplied traces for `trace_replay` stay out of git by default: a production
# trace leaks real workload patterns (arrival timing, session structure, context
# sizes) and must never land in a public repository by accident. The launcher payload
# packs from disk, not from git, so ignored traces still ride into the cluster.
#
# The pinned artifacts below are the exception: committed once, replayed identically
# on every run. See README.md for the regeneration policy.
*.jsonl
*.json
!agentx_32k_seed42.jsonl
!agentx_32k_config.json
